 "perceived_simulation": "[Messages]\n[learner]: Awesome, thanks — that sentence feels a lot clearer now.\n\nThe assignment also hints that there are “other important causes” of inflation besides money supply. I was thinking of adding a short second sentence about rising production costs (like higher oil prices) making goods more expensive.\n\nSomething like: \"Another important cause of inflation is when the costs of production go up, so firms raise their prices and this spreads through the economy.\"\n\nDoes that sound like a sensible way to put it, or would you tweak the wording a bit?",
 "response": "Yes—that's a sensible way to put it. A slightly tighter version: \"Another important cause—cost-push inflation—occurs when rising production costs (for example, higher oil prices, wages, or import costs) lead firms to raise prices, which is then passed on across the economy and raises the overall price level.\" If you have room, briefly naming an example like an oil shock can make the point even clearer."
 },
