 "perceived_simulation": "[Messages]\n[system]: After refining their explanation of inflation and adding a second sentence about cost-push inflation, the learner returns to get your take on how the full answer reads as a whole.\n[learner]: Okay, I think I’ve got my full answer now based on what we worked out.\n\nI’m planning to write:\n\n\"One main cause of inflation is when the central bank increases the money supply faster than the economy’s real output, so more money chases the same goods and services and prices rise. Another important cause—cost-push inflation—occurs when rising production costs, like higher oil prices or wages, lead firms to raise prices, which then pushes up the overall price level.\"\n\nFrom your perspective as a study buddy, does this sound clear and balanced for an undergrad IR essay, or would you tweak anything small (wording, length, order) before I hand it in?",
 "response": "That reads clear and balanced for an undergrad essay—nice work. Minor polish to tighten wording and parallel structure: \"One main cause of inflation is when the central bank expands the money supply faster than real output, so more money chases the same goods and services and prices rise.\" And: \"Another important cause—cost-push inflation—occurs when rising production costs (e.g., oil or wages) lead firms to raise prices, pushing up the overall price level.\" Either version should be fine to hand in; you can add a brief example if you want extra illustration."
 }
 ]
